WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.056 --> 00:00:04.888
♪ Persian ♪

00:00:14.433 --> 00:00:16.732
♪ Persian electronic ♪

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.740
[music continues]

00:01:41.882 --> 00:01:43.482
[music slowly fades]

00:01:54.819 --> 00:01:56.673
There's plenty of dark stuff
that happens here

00:01:56.673 --> 00:02:00.257
but there's a certain amount
of innocence in the culture.

00:02:01.004 --> 00:02:05.005
And maybe that's why McDonald's
hasn't completely taken over the land.

00:02:05.005 --> 00:02:06.698
I don't know what it is to be honest.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.573
In a way it's refreshing.

00:02:08.573 --> 00:02:10.923
There's some things that
are not refreshing here right now.

00:02:10.923 --> 00:02:12.656
The situation can be felt.

00:02:13.373 --> 00:02:17.644
But the way that people
have this authenticity.

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:20.616
I think that's a testament
to how special the culture is.

00:02:22.218 --> 00:02:24.009
Mona took me to the skate park.

00:02:24.009 --> 00:02:26.096
PETER: There's a woman
skateboarding scene here?

00:02:26.096 --> 00:02:27.096
Yes.

00:02:27.128 --> 00:02:32.428
You know, I like people who,
they express their inner-something.

00:02:32.428 --> 00:02:33.813
You know, inner-self.

00:02:33.813 --> 00:02:37.058
So there are lots of people
that are pretend living.

00:02:37.058 --> 00:02:41.004
You know, they're living their life
in a way that they don't like to

00:02:41.004 --> 00:02:46.630
but I respect people who just put
everything away, like money, everything.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:47.497
Right.

00:02:47.497 --> 00:02:49.891
They go around countries.

00:02:49.891 --> 00:02:53.076
I really love to come to the level.

00:02:53.566 --> 00:02:58.210
When you land a trick, (you) know,
you feel like you did a great job.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:01.208
You did it.
You've done it, you know?

00:03:01.208 --> 00:03:03.015
-It's over.
-Right.

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:07.074
And there are lots of bad (energies)
that go away from you

00:03:07.074 --> 00:03:09.211
and the adrilany...

00:03:09.211 --> 00:03:12.202
-Adrenaline?
-Adrenaline, yeah.

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:14.466
PETER: So Mona, we're in Tehran, right?

00:03:14.466 --> 00:03:15.466
Yeah.

00:03:15.954 --> 00:03:17.492
&lt;Very cool park in here.

00:03:17.777 --> 00:03:19.457
♪ Persian electronic ♪

00:03:24.862 --> 00:03:26.995
And there was this woman, Negin.

00:03:27.237 --> 00:03:29.771
She must have been maybe 17 years old.

00:03:36.855 --> 00:03:38.998
PETER: So focused, so driven.

00:03:38.998 --> 00:03:39.686
[skateboard clacking]

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:41.314
And she was out there in the skate park

00:03:41.314 --> 00:03:44.000
trying this one trick on the rail.

00:03:44.521 --> 00:03:50.091
She probably hit the ground
or the rail 35, 40 times.

00:03:51.184 --> 00:03:53.251
♪ rock with distorted guitar ♪

00:03:56.323 --> 00:03:58.590
[skateboard grinding and clacking]

00:04:08.164 --> 00:04:09.844
[man speaking Persian]

00:04:11.282 --> 00:04:12.779
[skateboard grinding and clacking]

00:04:12.826 --> 00:04:13.738
 PETER: Yeah!

00:04:19.113 --> 00:04:20.793
[skateboard clacking]

00:04:31.833 --> 00:04:33.009
That girl's tough.

00:04:33.009 --> 00:04:36.776
She hit her head, she'd hit
her knees, her elbows, her wrists.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.201
She'd get back up,
go at it again, go at it again.

00:04:39.201 --> 00:04:40.912
Again, again, again...

00:04:55.363 --> 00:04:56.963
[guitar intensifies]

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:04.500
PETER: Ooh!

00:05:06.352 --> 00:05:07.352
[giggles]

00:05:07.862 --> 00:05:10.638
Skating is a tough sport.

00:05:18.262 --> 00:05:19.567
[skateboard slides and clacks]

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:20.567
[Mona sighs]

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:25.120
MONA: Yo.

00:05:26.694 --> 00:05:28.491
-You need to give me a lesson.
-Yeah. [hands slap]

00:05:28.491 --> 00:05:31.291
I haven't skateboarded
since I was like 14.

00:05:31.412 --> 00:05:33.909
-How old are you?
-I'm 41.

00:05:33.909 --> 00:05:35.592
MONA: 41... Young.

00:05:36.549 --> 00:05:38.527
&lt;You're young, so young.

00:05:38.527 --> 00:05:40.622
So young, that's right, I like you.

00:05:40.622 --> 00:05:41.659
[both chuckling]

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:46.532
And they said,
"We feel so free when we can skate."

00:05:46.532 --> 00:05:48.212
♪ stand-up bass jazz ♪

00:05:55.615 --> 00:05:58.295
PETER: So tell me about skateboarding,
what were you just saying?

00:05:58.295 --> 00:06:01.787
It really feels good to skate in Iran

00:06:01.787 --> 00:06:05.169
because we girls don't really have
a lot of freedom here in Iran.

00:06:05.169 --> 00:06:08.506
Normal people don't accept
people who skate.

00:06:08.506 --> 00:06:10.684
-Uh-huh.
-Especially skateboard.

00:06:10.684 --> 00:06:14.623
PETER: And skating is, in my opinion,
it's like one of the hardest sports.

00:06:14.623 --> 00:06:16.075
-If not the hardest sport.
-For sure.

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:19.019
The moment that you land (it),
it's everything.

00:06:19.392 --> 00:06:20.422
It's everything?

00:06:20.422 --> 00:06:24.569
-You feel adrenaline, satisfaction?
-It's awesome.

00:06:24.569 --> 00:06:27.107
&lt;You might be the toughest person
I've ever met in my life.

00:06:29.078 --> 00:06:32.334
Thank you.
[all laughing]

00:06:32.334 --> 00:06:33.562
One more and then I'm done.

00:06:33.562 --> 00:06:36.162
I swear to God after this one I'm done.

00:06:36.941 --> 00:06:39.124
Mona, I need one more picture.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:41.146
These clouds and this light is perfect.

00:06:41.146 --> 00:06:43.013
I'm gonna take them up here.

00:06:43.384 --> 00:06:44.384
[giggling]

00:06:48.121 --> 00:06:49.801
[cheering and laughing]

00:06:51.668 --> 00:06:53.435
[hands slap]

00:06:55.701 --> 00:06:58.601
-See you again.
-See you again, keep skating.

00:07:01.319 --> 00:07:04.229
It's very expressive I would say.

00:07:04.455 --> 00:07:07.604
This guy was doing quite an intense dance.

00:07:07.604 --> 00:07:09.671
He's back at it again actually.

00:07:10.979 --> 00:07:11.979
♪ hip hop ♪

00:07:40.495 --> 00:07:41.495
♪ dub step ♪

00:07:54.672 --> 00:07:55.872
[Mona laughing]

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:57.509
[hands slap]

00:08:18.241 --> 00:08:23.466
I think Iranians are exceptional
at dividing politics and people.

00:08:24.072 --> 00:08:26.598
A lot of people might hate US policy

00:08:26.847 --> 00:08:30.217
but they don't hate American people.

00:08:30.378 --> 00:08:32.160
I've been told that time and time again.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:36.359
It's actually a very
pro-American country in that respect.

00:08:36.596 --> 00:08:38.539
Zero animosity.

00:08:38.898 --> 00:08:43.794
You can go to the US's closest
political ally, let's say the UK

00:08:43.896 --> 00:08:48.400
and you'll get more animosity
than if you go to a foe politically.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:51.600
And it's actually a good thing
to be American here.

00:08:51.788 --> 00:08:53.228
It's so confusing.

00:08:53.505 --> 00:08:54.492
♪ mellow guitar ♪

00:08:54.492 --> 00:08:58.632
When you travel alone and you have
a country and a culture warm up

00:08:58.632 --> 00:09:00.169
and come out and help

00:09:00.169 --> 00:09:02.153
and offer you their phones

00:09:02.564 --> 00:09:04.142
and help you in any way.

00:09:04.142 --> 00:09:06.200
Invite you to their family's homes.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:09.144
Invite you to dinners,
to sleep at their place.

00:09:09.423 --> 00:09:12.718
Whatever it might be,
that's the goal of travel.

00:09:13.225 --> 00:09:15.439
I want to say to the people of Iran

00:09:15.439 --> 00:09:18.743
you have a special culture
and you're a special people.

00:09:18.743 --> 00:09:20.942
It just gets the short end of the stick.

00:09:20.942 --> 00:09:25.166
How their voices... How the beauty
of this country doesn't get out.

00:09:25.916 --> 00:09:31.158
The human side of things
and so many people wanted to connect.

00:09:31.158 --> 00:09:34.561
Purely... Authentically... Yeah.

00:09:35.802 --> 00:09:38.586
I hope this captured some of that.

00:09:38.781 --> 00:09:40.461
♪ guitar and harmonica ♪

00:10:04.697 --> 00:10:06.286
[laughter]

00:10:33.629 --> 00:10:34.669
[music fades]

00:10:36.118 --> 00:10:37.984
♪ "Get Lucky" by Daft Punk ♪

